## Story Description
Add an optional dashed horizontal reference line to SpendAreaChart showing the period average. This makes monthly anomalies (spikes, dips) immediately visible without mental arithmetic. The line is labelled 'Avg' and shown in muted colour.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendAreaChart.tsx
- Add import: ReferenceLine from 'recharts' (add to the existing recharts import statement)
- Add optional prop showReferenceLine?: boolean (default false)
- When showReferenceLine is true, compute avgSpend: the arithmetic mean of all data[n].total_spend values. If data is empty skip rendering the line.
- Render a ReferenceLine inside the AreaChart: y={avgSpend} stroke='#94a3b8' strokeDasharray='4 4' strokeWidth={1.5}. Add a label prop: { value: 'Avg', position: 'insideTopRight', fontSize: 11, fill: '#94a3b8' }
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/OverviewPage.tsx — pass showReferenceLine={true} to the SpendAreaChart for the monthly trend chart
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

