## Story Description
Add two new visualisation sections above the individual recommendation cards: (1) a savings composition horizontal bar chart showing estimated savings per lever, giving instant portfolio composition view; (2) a row of lever summary cards (one per lever) showing total savings and count, which filter the recommendation cards when clicked. The existing Tabs navigation is replaced by the lever summary cards.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/RecommendationsPage.tsx
- Import SpendBarChart from @/components/charts. Import SEMANTIC_COLORS from '@/components/charts/constants'.
- Below the portfolio KPI row and confidence filter buttons, add a 'Savings by Lever' section: compute leverSummaries — an array of { lever: string, totalImpact: number, count: number } grouped from recommendations, sorted by totalImpact desc. Render as SpendBarChart with data=leverSummaries.map(l => ({ label: l.lever.replace(/_/g,' '), value: l.totalImpact })), title='Savings by Lever', horizontal={true}, valueFormatter={v => formatCurrency(v)}, showLabel={false}. Wrap in the standard chart container div 'border rounded-xl p-5 bg-card shadow-sm'.
- Below the savings bar chart, add a lever summary strip: a flex flex-wrap gap-3 row of cards, one per lever. Each card is a div with onClick handler, className that shows selected state: when selectedLever === lever use 'border-2 border-primary bg-primary/5 rounded-xl p-4 cursor-pointer', else 'border rounded-xl p-4 cursor-pointer hover:bg-muted/50'. Inside each card: lever name in text-sm font-semibold (humanized, replace _ with space), total impact in text-lg font-bold text-green-700, count in text-xs text-muted-foreground '{count} recommendations'.
- Add state: const [selectedLever, setSelectedLever] = useState<string | null>(null). Clicking a lever card toggles it: setSelectedLever(prev => prev === lever ? null : lever).
- Remove the existing Tabs / TabsList / TabsTrigger / TabsContent structure entirely. Replace it with a simple filtered list: const displayedRecs = (selectedLever ? filtered.filter(r => (r.lever ?? 'OTHER') === selectedLever) : filtered).sort((a,b) => (b.estimated_impact_aud ?? 0) - (a.estimated_impact_aud ?? 0)).
- Render displayedRecs as RecommendationCard components in a space-y-3 div. If displayedRecs is empty, show a p tag text-muted-foreground 'No recommendations match the current filters.'
- Remove Tabs imports since they are no longer needed.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

