## Story Description
Add a priority matrix scatter chart to the Recommendations page. X-axis is confidence (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW mapped to 0.9/0.6/0.3), Y-axis is estimated_impact_aud, bubble size is proportional to addressable_baseline. Each bubble is coloured by lever type. Hovering a bubble shows the recommendation context, type, and impact. This lets the user quickly spot high-confidence, high-impact opportunities.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/RecommendationsPage.tsx
- Import ScatterChart, Scatter, XAxis as RScatterXAxis, YAxis as RScatterYAxis, ZAxis, Tooltip as RScatterTooltip, ResponsiveContainer, Cell from 'recharts'. Use aliased names only if they conflict with existing imports.
- Create a new component inline or in the file: PriorityMatrix({ recommendations }: { recommendations: Recommendation[] }). This is a function component, not exported.
- Inside PriorityMatrix: map each recommendation to a scatter point: { x: confidence === 'HIGH' ? 0.9 : confidence === 'MEDIUM' ? 0.6 : 0.3, y: estimated_impact_aud ?? 0, z: Math.max((addressable_baseline ?? 0) / 1000, 100), label: context ?? '', type: type ?? '', impact: estimated_impact_aud ?? 0, lever: lever ?? 'OTHER' }
- Get unique levers from recommendations. Render one Scatter component per lever, each with a distinct fill color from CHART_COLORS (index by leverIndex). Pass data filtered to that lever.
- Wrap ScatterChart in ResponsiveContainer width='100%' height={280}.
- XAxis: type='number', domain=[0.2, 1.0], ticks=[0.3, 0.6, 0.9], tickFormatter mapping back to string: 0.3→'Low', 0.6→'Medium', 0.9→'High', label={{ value: 'Confidence', position: 'insideBottom', offset: -5, fontSize: 11 }}
- YAxis: type='number', tickFormatter={v => formatCurrency(v)}, label={{ value: 'Est. Savings', angle: -90, position: 'insideLeft', fontSize: 11 }}
- ZAxis: range=[40, 400] (controls min/max bubble size)
- Custom Tooltip: renders a div showing label, type (humanized), formatCurrency(impact)
- Render PriorityMatrix above the savings bar chart, wrapped in 'border rounded-xl p-5 bg-card shadow-sm'. Title as h3 className='section-header': 'Priority Matrix — Impact vs. Confidence'. Only render if recommendations.length > 0.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

