## Story Description
Three focused improvements to the Data Quality page: sort checks by severity (RED first, then AMBER, then GREEN) so the most critical issues appear first; add a visual Progress bar to each check card below the percentage; add an 'Affects recommendations' badge to the two checks that directly degrade recommendation quality.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/DataQualityPage.tsx — sort the checks array before rendering: const SEVERITY_ORDER: Record<string, number> = { RED: 0, AMBER: 1, GREEN: 2 }. Sort: checks.sort((a,b) => (SEVERITY_ORDER[a.status] ?? 2) - (SEVERITY_ORDER[b.status] ?? 2)).
- Edit file: frontend/src/components/dashboard/DiagnosticsCheckCard.tsx
- Add import: import { Progress } from '@/components/ui/progress'
- Add optional prop affectsRecommendations?: boolean
- In the card body, after the description paragraph, add a Progress component: value={Math.min(value_pct, 100)}. Style the progress indicator colour by status: for GREEN use default, for AMBER add className='[&>div]:bg-amber-500', for RED add className='[&>div]:bg-red-500'. Wrap in a div className='mt-2'.
- When affectsRecommendations is true, render a Badge below the description: className='text-xs bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 border-blue-200 mt-1' with text '⚠ Affects recommendations'.
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/DataQualityPage.tsx — when rendering DiagnosticsCheckCard, pass affectsRecommendations={['missing_category', 'low_confidence_category'].includes(c.check_name)}.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

